  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115846",
      "title": "An Easier Way of Setting Up Custom Two-Way Binding",
      "lectureOrder": 149,
      "videoOrder": 141,
      "sourceHash": "d79d29212ba919c08eeb905d7d3a80b59881bcb44955b0e116fb56971f20ca34",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 2.82,
          "en": "So that's how you can set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.82,
          "end": 5.85,
          "en": "custom two-way binding for your own property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.85,
          "end": 8.43,
          "en": "in your own Component with the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.43,
          "end": 11.01,
          "en": "and output decorators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.01,
          "end": 14.67,
          "en": "But depending on the Angular version you're using,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.67,
          "end": 17.19,
          "en": "you can actually use an alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.19,
          "end": 20.61,
          "en": "more modern, and simpler syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.61,
          "end": 25.61,
          "en": "Specifically, you must be using Angular version 17.2",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.65,
          "end": 29.31,
          "en": "or later, and if you're doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.31,
          "end": 33.84,
          "en": "you can set up this two-way binding in a way easier way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.84,
          "end": 37.17,
          "en": "You still need to create the two-way bindable property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.17,
          "end": 39.39,
          "en": "in the Component that should receive it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.39,
          "end": 41.91,
          "en": "so here in the RectComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.91,
          "end": 46.53,
          "en": "but then you assign an initial value to that property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.53,
          "end": 49.803,
          "en": "that's created with help of the model function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.15,
          "end": 53.25,
          "en": "and that is a function that must be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.25,
          "end": 56.13,
          "en": "from angular/core, and that's only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.13,
          "end": 60.603,
          "en": "if you are using Angular 17.2 or newer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 66.81,
          "en": "This model function will in the end make this size property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.81,
          "end": 70.17,
          "en": "two-way bindable, and it saves you the effort",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.17,
          "end": 73.053,
          "en": "of creating separate inputs and outputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.01,
          "end": 76.41,
          "en": "Now, you should still let Angular know which kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.41,
          "end": 79.293,
          "en": "of data will be handled by model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.19,
          "end": 83.78999999999999,
          "en": "and you can actually also call a required method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.78999999999999,
          "end": 85.89,
          "en": "on this model here to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.89,
          "end": 88.11,
          "en": "that some value must be passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.11,
          "end": 91.203,
          "en": "for this size property to this Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.28,
          "end": 95.46000000000001,
          "en": "You of course don't have to make it required, but you can,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.46000000000001,
          "end": 97.74000000000001,
          "en": "and since I used required before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.74000000000001,
          "end": 101.22,
          "en": "I'll also use it here on model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.22,
          "end": 103.77000000000001,
          "en": "Now, with this setup like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.77000000000001,
          "end": 106.35300000000001,
          "en": "size will be a so-called ModelSignal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108,
          "end": 110.75999999999999,
          "en": "So it says Signal in the end, and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.75999999999999,
          "end": 113.88499999999999,
          "en": "you can use it in the template like all those Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.88499999999999,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "by executing it like a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 120.03,
          "en": "to have Angular set up a subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.03,
          "end": 124.02,
          "en": "so that whenever the value managed by that Signal changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 127.5,
          "en": "this Component's template here will be reevaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.5,
          "end": 130.923,
          "en": "and updated automatically by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132,
          "end": 135.75,
          "en": "So that's how we must use size in the template now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.75,
          "end": 139.14,
          "en": "and we also need to change this code in onReset,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.14,
          "end": 141.66,
          "en": "because instead of emitting some event here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.66,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "you now simply must update this Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 149.25,
          "en": "like you always update Signals by using the set method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.25,
          "end": 153.123,
          "en": "or by using the update method, both works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.14,
          "end": 156.03,
          "en": "and here, I want to use set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.03,
          "end": 160.8,
          "en": "and set this to a new value where width is 200",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.8,
          "end": 163.713,
          "en": "and height is 100, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.48,
          "end": 169.14,
          "en": "And that's all, this will update the Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.14,
          "end": 171.93,
          "en": "and Angular will then automatically be notified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.93,
          "end": 174.15,
          "en": "about this update in the Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.15,
          "end": 177.63,
          "en": "that provided the value for the two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.63,
          "end": 180.12,
          "en": "so in the AppComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.12,
          "end": 183.33,
          "en": "and it doesn't matter whether you are using a Signal here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.33,
          "end": 187.71,
          "en": "or not, you can absolutely use a non-Signal value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.71,
          "end": 192.71,
          "en": "and pass that as a value for this model-based size property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.75,
          "end": 195.54,
          "en": "and it will still work fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 195.54,
          "end": 198.78,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could also be working with a Signal here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.78,
          "end": 200.1,
          "en": "it doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 203.76,
          "en": "Angular will make sure that it works either way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.76,
          "end": 205.98,
          "en": "Well, and therefore with that, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.98,
          "end": 207.87,
          "en": "if you go back and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.87,
          "end": 212.87,
          "en": "you can still change those dimensions from inside here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 213.42000000000002,
          "end": 215.91,
          "en": "as you can see from inside these input fields,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.91,
          "end": 219.54,
          "en": "but if you then click on this, it's still also sent back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.54,
          "end": 222.99,
          "en": "to that AppComponent and it is being reset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.99,
          "end": 226.47,
          "en": "So with that, the two-way binding still works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.47,
          "end": 228.75,
          "en": "but now with even less code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.75,
          "end": 231.603,
          "en": "thanks to this modern model function.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
